# The template `stack.sh` seeds `.env.local` from on first run.
#
# **Secrets stay in the repository root `.env`** — gitignored, same rule as everywhere
# else in this project. At minimum that file needs `VAULT_ENT_LICENSE`; model keys,
# Auth0, and Build/Propose App seeding are optional and gate specific features rather
# than bring-up. This file holds ports and local-stack toggles only; comments below
# name the root-`.env` keys each feature needs.

# ── Identity (feature 023) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The development provider the MCP surface verifies against when no Auth0 domain is set.
# Started as a compose service; the surface reaches it at host.docker.internal.
DEV_IDP_PORT=8090

# ── Northbound MCP surface (feature 019) ─────────────────────────────────────
MCP_SURFACE_PORT=8083

# ── Portal (feature 012) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Started with the stack by default; uses TLS on loopback (self-signed by the control-plane CA).
PORTAL_PORT=8082

# ── Optional model posture (027+) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset leaves `ask` honest — the surface refuses before calling a vendor rather than
# answering from the corpus alone. Set in repo `.env`, not here:
#   ASK_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet@5
#   RELEVANCE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus@5
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=…          # vendor key; also gitignored root `.env` only

# ── Build / Propose — authoring publish (038 / 041 / 047, ADR-0062) ───────────
# Portal Build opens a PR from a Nomad proposer task. Host `gh auth` does NOT reach
# that container. Publishing mints a short-lived GitHub App installation token from
# Vault; a personal token is refused on purpose.
#
# Operator prerequisites (set in repo-root `.env` where noted; seed Vault once):
#
#   1. A GitHub App with Contents + Pull requests (read/write) on the target repo.
#   2. Identifiers in root `.env` (not secrets — terraform uses the same names):
#        AUTHORING_APP_ID=<numeric App ID>
#        AUTHORING_INSTALLATION_ID=<installation id on that repo/org>
#        PROPOSE_OWNED_REPOSITORIES=owner/repo[,owner/other]
#      `portal-up` passes owned repos into the API job; without them Build fails closed.
#   3. App private key in Vault ONLY — never in `.env`, never in git, never in chat:
#        vault kv put -mount=harness-authority authoring/vcs-app \
#          app_id="$AUTHORING_APP_ID" \
#          installation_id="$AUTHORING_INSTALLATION_ID" \
#          private_key=@/path/to/app.pem
#      Path: harness-authority/data/authoring/vcs-app. Terraform creates the path with
#      placeholders (`SET-OUT-OF-BAND`); an apply ignores later operator writes.
#   4. Proposer env RUN_VCS_INSTALLATION must equal AUTHORING_INSTALLATION_ID (wired
#      when registering authoring-tier). Empty → "no installation named for publishing".
#
# Without (2)–(4), analyzer may still author; proposer cannot open a PR.
# Full local-estate install guide is still owed; until then see
# specs/041-authoring-becomes-reachable/quickstart.md.

# ── Tenant ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written into repo `.env` by `make dev-up` when absent. Override here only if you
# need a non-default before the first enclave apply.
# HARNESS_DEFAULT_TENANT=tenant-local
